<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 2.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 2.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on December 31. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		   P/E	 Close</p>
<p>1   Tourism Asset	 3666.67    1.10</p>
<p>2   Portman Min	    374.60    2.36</p>
<p>3   Niugini Min	    223.02    3.10</p>
<p>4   Mayne Nickless	 189.85    8.60</p>
<p>5   Colonial Coml	  124.04    2.27</p>
<p>6   Adel Bton Cement     123.91    1.71</p>
<p>7   Forrestania Gold	87.81    2.45</p>
<p>8   Westral Forest	  85.14    2.35</p>
<p>9   Countrywide-PP	  83.21    1.14</p>
<p>10  Herald Rsc		82.30    0.93</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p>1   Dominion Min	     2.16    0.94</p>
<p>2   Consol Rutile	    3.19    0.90</p>
<p>3   Computer Power	   3.76    3.85</p>
<p>4   Premier Inv		4.23    0.75</p>
<p>5   Queensland Cotton	5.77    4.38</p>
<p>6   Parbury Ltd		6.25    0.74</p>
<p>7   BTR Plc		    6.45    6.00</p>
